{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:e43646e53e2f94ac","name":"Aurek Tactical Strikefighter","source":{"id":"source:reference-e43646e53e2f94ac","title":"Aurek Tactical Strikefighter","revision":16030,"timestamp":"2024-08-18T00:53:32Z","sha256":"a9a5fdf45b96e2546e75897490be4024ff5d00c4db9018400529abb695c84cf1","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=16030","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Aurek%20Tactical%20Strikefighter&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-e43646e53e2f94ac","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Old Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Old_Republic","referenceId":"reference:6517b7e15507b001"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["When the Republic Navy's coffers began to overflow with credits during The Restoration, the Navy sponsored one of the greatest engineering contests in years. More than three dozen shipwrights were solicited to submit designs for the \"Generation Tomorrow Starfighter,\" intended to replace the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Star Saber XC-01 Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Star_Saber_XC-01_Starfighter","referenceId":"reference:32f8384f6e671507"}," as the stock Starship in the Navy's arsenal. The winning design- coproduced with the Republic though its Republic Fleet Systems consortium of manufacturers- is a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"}," for the ages.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The 9.2-meter-long Aurek Tactical Strikefighter combines speed and maneuverability, with the ability to deal surprising amounts of damage. Ease of refueling and rearmament make the Aurek Tactical Strikefighter ideal for ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ship"}," squadrons. And their simple fuselage minimizes production time, to such an extent that the Republic frequently foregoes all but the most minor repair work, choosing instead to ship out new Strikefighters. This results in many scrapped Aurek Tactical Strikefighters finding their way into civilian use.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The chevron-shaped fighter's wings can be reconfigured in different attack positions, one of which resembles the Aurebesh letter that inspired the craft's name.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Skilled)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Aurek Tactical Strikefighter Statistics (CL 11)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Huge ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +10; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +6\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 18 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 12), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 25; +4 Armor, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicular Combat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicular_Combat","referenceId":"reference:31246426131b3457"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},": 110; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Reduction"],"href":"https:/